===== quadcam-cli  --help
Import FPV clips (analog DVR, DJI): stage, date, name, convert, verify, share, format

Usage: quadcam-cli [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  cards     List removable volumes: cards (with their source, analog or DJI) and radio log sources
  scan      List the clips on a volume or folder without copying anything
  stage     Copy every clip off a card or folder into staging and start a new session
  analyze   Probe staged clips, recover half-written ones, make thumbnails
  dates     Date clips from radio logs, and override dates and times per clip
  show      Show the current session: clips, plans, results
  clear     Forget the current session and delete the session file (staged copies stay)
  moments   Show each clip's moments (radio-log sticks and dead air), keep ranges and cuts
  profiles  Aircraft profiles: list (default), save, delete, set the default
  places    Saved places: list (default), search by address or name, save, delete
  settings  The app's settings: show (default) or set
  modules   Tools QuadCam downloads from their upstream (ffmpeg, esptool): list (default), check for newer pins, install, remove
  meta      Set metadata on clips: profile, location, keywords, author
  cut       Set the cut ranges of one clip. Each exports as an extra <name>_cutN file on import
  import    Convert and verify every non-skipped clip
  verify    Re-verify outputs: the session's (default) or one file against its source
  photos    Add videos to Photos: given files, or the session's verified outputs
  eject     Make a card safe to remove: unmount it, or eject a disk that is not a card (mount point or /dev/diskN; default: the session's card)
  format    Erase the session's card with its source's file system (FAT32 for analog). Runs every guard and refuses without all of --device, --volume-uuid and --yes. With --prep, erase a card with no session instead (card prep: every clip on it must be in the library; a DJI goggles card becomes exFAT); --plan then needs --mount
  library   The library: list, rate, rename, edit (details, aircraft, date, time), cut, trash, Photos
  gear      Gear: the radio, flight controllers, goggles and cards QuadCam knows and sees
  mcp       Run the MCP server on stdio
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
  -V, --version         Print version
