===== quadcam-cli meta --help
Set metadata on clips: profile, location, keywords, author

Usage: quadcam-cli meta [OPTIONS] <IDS>...

Arguments:
  <IDS>...  Clip ids, or `all`

Options:
      --json                 Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --profile <PROFILE>    Aircraft profile name ("" to fall back to the log's model, then the default)
      --place <PLACE>        A saved place name
      --session <FILE>       Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --location <LOCATION>  LAT,LON in decimal degrees
      --clear-location       
      --keywords <KEYWORDS>  Comma-separated keywords; replaces the clip's own
      --author <AUTHOR>      
  -h, --help                 Print help
===== quadcam-cli cut --help
Set the cut ranges of one clip. Each exports as an extra <name>_cutN file on import

Usage: quadcam-cli cut [OPTIONS] <ID> [RANGES]...

Arguments:
  <ID>         
  [RANGES]...  Ranges in clip seconds or m:ss, for example 12.5-18 or 1:02-1:10. Replaces the list

Options:
      --json                     Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --keep                     Use the suggested keep ranges (the clip without its dead air)
      --clear                    Remove every cut
      --session <FILE>           Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --by-flight                Add one cut per radio-log flight (the armed range plus up to 2 s each side)
      --log-offset <LOG_OFFSET>  Seconds into the clip where the radio log's first armed row falls
      --removed <REMOVED>        For cuts already exported that the new list drops: keep their files (as clips of their own) or move them to the Trash [possible values: keep, trash]
  -h, --help                     Print help
===== quadcam-cli import --help
Convert and verify every non-skipped clip

Usage: quadcam-cli import [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json                Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --plan <FILE>         JSON plan: {"clips":[{"id":0,"name":"..","date":"YYYY-MM-DD","time":"HH:MM","note":"..","skip":false}]}
      --name <ID=NAME>      Short name for one clip: ID=NAME. Repeatable
      --session <FILE>      Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --note <ID=NOTE>      Note for one clip: ID=NOTE. Repeatable
      --date <ID=DATE>      Date for one clip: ID=YYYY-MM-DD. Repeatable
      --time <ID=HH:MM>     Time of day for one clip: ID=HH:MM ("ID=" for noon). Repeatable
      --skip <ID>           Skip a clip. Repeatable
      --unskip <ID>         Import a clip that was skipped. Repeatable
      --separate <ID>       Import the files of a split recording (ID: its first file) as clips of their own. Repeatable
      --join <ID>           Import the files of a split recording (ID: its first file) as one clip. Repeatable
      --cut <ID=START-END>  Add a cut range to a clip: ID=START-END (seconds or m:ss). Repeatable
      --format <FORMAT>     [possible values: mp4, mov]
      --encoder <ENCODER>   [possible values: videotoolbox, x264]
      --output <OUTPUT>     Output folder (default: ~/Movies/quadcam)
      --keep-originals      
      --add-time            Add HHMM to names of clips dated from a radio log
      --add-to-photos       
      --album <ALBUM>       Photos album (default "Drone"; "" for library only)
      --keep-clips          Keep every clip on the card this run, even when delete_clips_after_import is on
  -h, --help                Print help
===== quadcam-cli verify --help
Re-verify outputs: the session's (default) or one file against its source

Usage: quadcam-cli verify [OPTIONS] [OUTPUT]

Arguments:
  [OUTPUT]  

Options:
      --json             Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --source <SOURCE>  Source AVI for a one-off check (frames, duration, streams)
      --session <FILE>   Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help             Print help
===== quadcam-cli photos --help
Add videos to Photos: given files, or the session's verified outputs

Usage: quadcam-cli photos [OPTIONS] [FILES]...

Arguments:
  [FILES]...  

Options:
      --album <ALBUM>   
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --dry-run         Check the files and report; add nothing
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
===== quadcam-cli eject --help
Make a card safe to remove: unmount it, or eject a disk that is not a card (mount point or /dev/diskN; default: the session's card)

Usage: quadcam-cli eject [OPTIONS] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  

Options:
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
===== quadcam-cli format --help
Erase the session's card with its source's file system (FAT32 for analog). Runs every guard and refuses without all of --device, --volume-uuid and --yes. With --prep, erase a card with no session instead (card prep: every clip on it must be in the library; a DJI goggles card becomes exFAT); --plan then needs --mount

Usage: quadcam-cli format [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --device <DEVICE>            Whole-disk device of the card, for example /dev/disk4
      --json                       Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>             Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --volume-uuid <VOLUME_UUID>  
      --label <LABEL>              Volume name (default DVR)
      --yes                        
      --plan                       Only print what would be erased; runs every guard
      --prep                       Card prep: a card with no session, new or with every clip in the library
      --mount <MOUNT>              Card prep: the card's mount point, for --plan
  -h, --help                       Print help
===== quadcam-cli library --help
The library: list, rate, rename, edit (details, aircraft, date, time), cut, trash, Photos

Usage: quadcam-cli library [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list               List clips, newest first
  rate               Set stars (0 to 5, 0 clears) and pick or reject flags. Written into the files too
  rebuild            Make the index again from the files (also adopts an existing export folder)
  rename             Rename a clip's file, its cuts and its original
  edit               Change a clip's note, keywords, author, place, aircraft profile, date or time
  cut                Set a clip's cut ranges, and write the new ones with --export
  apply-name-format  Rename clips to the name date format setting (YYYY-MM-DD or YY.MM.DD), with their cuts and originals. Default: every clip. Folders stay as they are
  match-logs         Match radio logs to library clips by shape. Reports only; --apply writes the flight numbers and moments of "matched" clips (and "likely" ones named by id)
  trash              Move clips, with their cuts and originals, to the Trash
  photos             Add clips and their cuts to Photos
  help               Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
===== quadcam-cli library list --help
List clips, newest first

Usage: quadcam-cli library list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json                     Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
  -q, --query <QUERY>            Words that must all appear in the name, note, place, aircraft, keywords or file
      --group <GROUP>            all, last_import, moments, picks, rejected, not_in_photos [possible values: all, last_import, moments, picks, rejected, not_in_photos]
      --session <FILE>           Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --day <DAY>                One flying day (YYYY-MM-DD)
      --place <PLACE>            
      --aircraft <AIRCRAFT>      
      --min-rating <MIN_RATING>  At least this many stars
  -h, --help                     Print help
===== quadcam-cli library rate --help
Set stars (0 to 5, 0 clears) and pick or reject flags. Written into the files too

Usage: quadcam-cli library rate [OPTIONS] <IDS>...

