===== quadcam-cli library edit --help
Change a clip's note, keywords, author, place, aircraft profile, date or time

Usage: quadcam-cli library edit [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  

Options:
      --json                 Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --note <NOTE>          
      --keywords <KEYWORDS>  Comma-separated; replaces the list
      --session <FILE>       Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --author <AUTHOR>      
      --place <PLACE>        A saved place name ("" removes the location)
      --location <LOCATION>  LAT,LON in decimal degrees
      --profile <PROFILE>    Aircraft profile name ("" removes the profile's details). Rewrites make, model, aircraft and the profile's keywords
      --date <DATE>          New flying day (YYYY-MM-DD). Moves the clip, its cuts and its original
      --time <TIME>          Time of day (HH:MM, "" for noon). Without it a new date keeps the clip's time
  -h, --help                 Print help
===== quadcam-cli library cut --help
Set a clip's cut ranges, and write the new ones with --export

Usage: quadcam-cli library cut [OPTIONS] <ID> [RANGES]...

Arguments:
  <ID>         
  [RANGES]...  Ranges in seconds or m:ss. Replaces the list

Options:
      --clear              
      --json               Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --by-flight          Add one cut per radio-log flight (the armed range plus up to 2 s each side)
      --session <FILE>     Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
      --removed <REMOVED>  For exported cuts the new list drops: keep their files or move them to the Trash [possible values: keep, trash]
      --export             Write the cuts that are not files yet
  -h, --help               Print help
