      --album <ALBUM>   
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
===== quadcam-cli gear --help
Gear: the radio, flight controllers, goggles and cards QuadCam knows and sees

Usage: quadcam-cli gear [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status          The gear folder, the Gear settings, and the devices plugged in now
  devices         Saved devices: list (default), save a name or aircraft, forget
  fc              A Betaflight flight controller: identify, read, check, board notes, USB timer
  osd             An FC's OSD layout per OSD profile, drawn on its grid and checked for overlaps and cells off screen. Reads a dump or diff file
  osd-edit        Stages OSD moves, toggles or a profile copy for an FC (one "OSD layout" change)
  card            An EdgeTX card: models, the selected model, the radio clock; `preview` checks edits
  map             The switch map: what each radio control does on the radio and the FC, per position. Reads an EdgeTX card or model file and a Betaflight dump; --live marks the positions now
  radio           The radio in USB Joystick mode now: buttons, axes, channel values
  sim             The sim: a radio's calibration, the defaults an aircraft gives it
  flights         Flights from the radio logs: measures, pack, place, clip. `set` and `folders`
  report          The session report for a day, else the last import's days
  preflight       The "Pack up" check: packs charged, radio model, card space, backups, cards still in
  packs           Packs with their history, pack types, the charging notes
  crashes         The crash and repair log: list, `save`, `delete`
  backup          Back up a radio card or an FC (the FC reboots); `show`, `diff` and `pin` a backup
  backups         Backups, newest first
  storage         The gear folder's size per device; --prune thins backups; --export writes folders
  import-backups  Import an old backup folder: radio card copies, FC diff/dump files, LOGS folders
  card-check      Check a card's file system (diskutil verifyVolume, read-only); --log lists past checks
  card-repair     Repair a card whose latest check failed: a backup first, the repair, a check after
  changes         Staged changes waiting to be applied (--history adds the rest)
  stage           Stage FC settings: raw CLI lines (--cli FILE) or --set NAME=VALUE. Writes nothing to the FC
  discard         Discard a staged change. It stays in the history
  restore         Stage a backup's settings back as a change. An FC backup restores its `dump all`; a radio card backup needs the files to put back (`--path`, repeat for more)
  update          Change a staged change's status (draft, ready, try, read_first), title, note or order
  keep            Keep an applied Try change
  revert          Stage a restore of the backup an applied change took. The change becomes Reverted when the restore verifies
  copy            Copy settings between quads: `--plan` shows the checks and the diff; without it the settings are staged as one change for the target FC
  card-mount      Mount an unmounted radio card to browse it; it unmounts after --minutes (10)
  card-unmount    Unmount a radio card (Done)
  apply           Apply a staged change to the FC: `--plan` shows the checks, diff and digest; `--digest D --yes` backs up, writes, saves, reads back and verifies
  stop            Stop a running backup or card check (its handle from `gear status`)
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print one JSON object: {"ok":true,"result":...} or {"ok":false,"error":{...}}
      --session <FILE>  Session file (default: ~/Library/Caches/app.quadcam/session.json)
  -h, --help            Print help
===== quadcam-cli gear status --help
The gear folder, the Gear settings, and the devices plugged in now

Usage: quadcam-cli gear status [OPTIONS]

